<title>INDIA: India sets 25 pct 1997/98 export growth target.</title>
<headline>India sets 25 pct 1997/98 export growth target.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Commerce Ministry on Tuesday set a 25 percent target rate of growth for exports in fiscal 1997/98 (April-March), the Press Trust of India said.</p>
<p>The news agency said the target was agreed upon during a meeting between Commerce Minister Bolla Buli Ramaiah and representatives of export promotion councils. It gave no other details.</p>
<p>India's exports grew by just 4.01 percent in 1996/97 after a spurt of 21.38 percent in the previous year.</p>
</text>
